                <l xml:id="m-d7764803-fe65-461c-b901-c1315c9948e9" facs="#m-7522eca7-0054-42b8-be92-7a21bfe4027c" label="ambiguous">580</l><l xml:id="m-cb2edbbc-0e7e-45ec-aef7-c12bcd4e570b" facs="#m-75023971-bf5e-4c2b-83a4-65ab4758f616" label="text-like">Second Sunday of the Passion</l><l xml:id="m-81f36e62-7182-4072-8250-a5488a54838d" facs="#m-3bddec6b-b151-4fbb-907a-6997cb9c97b6" label="text-like">4. If the faithful are not already holding their palms, these are placed on</l><l xml:id="m-34f4ef16-f818-4c87-8826-53953f7a56d9" facs="#m-ccee4587-131a-4108-81ea-d0ca8577e45e" label="text-like">a table which is covered vith a vohite cloth and placed in a convemient place</l><l xml:id="m-46ba8416-4040-4647-a47f-34fa2de67fca" facs="#m-e0e83120-7788-480a-8543-a35bb372b778" label="text-like">in the sanctuary so that the people can see it.</l><l xml:id="m-c8186919-f4dd-4c74-bb42-fcebb8f383e5" facs="#m-2cc26cc3-c3c9-4dc0-a507-bf57a49dea42" label="text-like">5. When everything is ready, the celebrant and the sacred ministers</l><l xml:id="m-fa33ddd5-7dd0-4f0f-beff-7669de9d3a1d" facs="#m-c215b976-5100-4c6f-9981-6549f79be7f2" label="lyrics-like">lor serversll̀ genuflect or bow to the altar as usual, and go behind the table,</l><l xml:id="m-14a28498-9bc9-4857-8b78-d222dc3759db" facs="#m-c60c2fa5-8ca2-4c88-af29-7eebd4601a6c" label="text-like">facing the people.</l><l xml:id="m-3af2c96f-2534-42fc-b292-e3e1c3e2acdb" facs="#m-a6fc3115-8cd7-450f-b022-4cc82feaed66" label="text-like">While this is taking place, the follouing antiphon is sung:</l><l xml:id="m-99b320d1-c623-4b33-90c9-34db826c61e4" facs="#m-943152db-f1bc-40ed-9138-4ad68fd4ff2d" label="ambiguous">Ant.</l><l xml:id="m-42c9ad5d-e880-412b-9365-45fb7a112c56" facs="#m-37307196-8216-4205-9663-036f4542fd6e" label="lyrics-like">LOsánna“ fi-li-o Dávid: benedí-ctus qui vé-nit</l><l xml:id="m-9a4f9bea-25f5-4509-9c28-466ce9d9d3ef" facs="#m-a38e1d37-12a9-4b67-905e-318e23df4e5b" label="lyrics-like">in nómine Dómimni.</l><l xml:id="m-c6b82936-a2c1-4a82-a2ce-f95cb978b92b" facs="#m-b2a4a4e9-f4e0-46a7-9e80-d8f933e3bdd9" label="lyrics-like">el : Hosánna</l><l xml:id="m-d4c6f7d5-ebb9-47f5-a04a-e87f1a1eeb74" facs="#m-54572836-8e64-4b1d-9bef-8fd58566110e" label="ambiguous">Rex Is- ra¬</l><l xml:id="m-0d5fa610-f934-443e-bb29-b212c92adc52" facs="#m-c53f1be7-516c-4c99-98ec-657617b3c72e" label="ambiguous">in</l><l xml:id="m-ae4ee4bc-c586-4aaf-96bf-1213eaf39388" facs="#m-90fa18a4-fc38-4d9f-b5d5-8b6b103b9900" label="lyrics-like">excél-sis.</l><l xml:id="m-05bf66b2-a9b7-4644-9926-e253489376a4" facs="#m-f54a302c-ba49-443c-806a-af4f79ea7631" label="text-like">6. Then the celebrant, with his hands joined, blesses the palms, singing</l><l xml:id="m-55bb0970-3168-496c-9550-4368d495d9f5" facs="#m-bd35b4dd-4900-46d0-ab60-06c3ce865ae1" label="text-like">the Collect to the ferial E tone (or the simple ancient tone).</l><l xml:id="m-a79a7dd6-2d3b-4f77-8edd-68da43c1c309" facs="#m-4116b84d-f564-40d6-af87-e4e2152eeac5" label="lyrics-like">V. Dóminus vobiscum.</l><l xml:id="m-86b4de1e-76b6-49fc-b908-a499aa4c7137" facs="#m-309dd91c-ffe0-475d-9f62-aea2f2d0c29d" label="ambiguous">All answer:</l><l xml:id="m-74903298-2794-4cae-9d02-b6e7ede97baa" facs="#m-82f3108f-ec0e-4a00-a6c3-799fa4733d5e" label="lyrics-like">R. Et cum spíritu túo.</l><l xml:id="m-586bfaa9-d1a3-4ede-b78f-a236b3c67499" facs="#m-1f372f62-5137-4e54-8037-293992d359cd" label="text-like">7. In the following Collect the celebrant should say: these branches of</l><l xml:id="m-a5fb1b0c-d2f0-45e8-99be-e2b6e4625e19" facs="#m-865405e8-66ac-4cd4-a5b6-7421e0e3fefb" label="text-like">palms, or these branches of olives, or these branches of trees, or these</l><l xml:id="m-d0cd3ef3-5f50-4c60-8a27-7b1601369f2a" facs="#m-cd247ce6-bd95-4144-b242-22fe2825c0a5" label="text-like">branches of palms and olives, or these branches of palms (olives) and</l><l xml:id="m-52fa08aa-ad9d-4f95-a218-b926dc56cec1" facs="#m-da26eb80-57e7-4c76-89c4-3d86e2455691" label="text-like">other trees.</l><l xml:id="m-d490649c-ae09-49b3-b5ca-a5218e7c9c5f" facs="#m-b51593c1-0d1f-47aa-a333-64b6d2cc078b" label="lyrics-like">Orémus.</l><l xml:id="m-36a28903-1bf9-43e6-9f89-5b40d916c2cc" facs="#m-19c22c71-a33d-4951-990b-4966b8df502e" label="text-like">Prayer</l><l xml:id="m-711fc592-f241-4a06-b1cc-1e6e50961bb9" facs="#m-b4e29b70-8756-4aed-ac4d-c8d5bb5f23d7" label="lyrics-like">DEne† dic, quaésumus, Dó-¡ hoc spirituáliter summa devo¬</l><l xml:id="m-2e3fa444-3add-4e66-882c-50bbd6a6d27c" facs="#m-1c362c4f-14da-4e65-b5ad-abc1fcb09dd7" label="lyrics-like">D mine, hos palmárum (or</l><l xml:id="m-629f7ec6-7e54-4bfb-9a12-d37be3a41dd6" facs="#m-442e1575-b41d-4589-be01-a7a5b03a29f8" label="lyrics-like">tióne perficiat, * de hoste victó¬</l><l xml:id="m-c79e34fc-9d83-46a9-9117-d5eebf0b0e20" facs="#m-b4d52b2d-d36b-4a5a-8faa-874ce2bba056" label="lyrics-like">olivárum or aliárum árborum)</l><l xml:id="m-8e4fbc8e-dbc0-4803-bcc7-b40fa6333e52" facs="#m-0451c4e6-a840-4ae8-a051-f5192fc11513" label="lyrics-like">riam reportándo et opus miseri¬</l><l xml:id="m-f7dfda1f-e057-4072-a2fb-32a560843429" facs="#m-ddd124f1-9a5a-4dd6-a415-5b01e1a7f589" label="lyrics-like">ramos: f et praesta; ut, quod córdiae summópere diligéndo.</l><l xml:id="m-49176958-4594-4d42-8b6f-aeca2cccd66f" facs="#m-9629e2f1-efc8-4cc5-99c7-c8016c022556" label="lyrics-like">pópulus tuus in tui veneratiónem! Per Dóminum nostrum Jesum</l><l xml:id="m-ed5f818c-ea7f-4c88-bf21-b56f84c42819" facs="#m-6a56029e-a596-4b89-b725-58dfd87526a6" label="lyrics-like">hodiérno die corporáliter agit, Christum.</l><l xml:id="m-4d267ab5-a08b-4270-a3db-ba36cf4e8e7f" facs="#m-47353734-70cc-4205-a39b-d528422504e9" label="text-like">8. Then the celebrant, saving nothing, sprinbles three times the palms on the</l><l xml:id="m-c9a1d3c8-fb80-4579-8b08-50d7ce83847c" facs="#m-3c9a0ffd-ae98-4595-bf83-6f17445f8245" label="text-like">table, then, at the rail, those that the people, as said above, may have in their</l><l xml:id="m-8d999e63-1910-47cd-8f0c-20a2f33a2301" facs="#m-724096aa-14bd-494c-a452-f922e64eb8f7" label="text-like">hands; or he may pass through the aisles of the church.</l><l xml:id="m-808dba29-c801-4a07-a0e6-023def0bc7ab" facs="#m-977a7b53-ce53-442a-92ba-3a61ee6b4457" label="text-like">9. Next the celebrant puts incense in the thurible and blesses it; then he</l><l xml:id="m-bb2d80d7-70b1-4ec3-a574-cf4989979bc8" facs="#m-46a6d80b-da07-4724-8776-d5565c610ead" label="lyrics-like">censes the palms on the tãble, finally, from the rail (or the aisles) those held</l><l xml:id="m-785e69c6-3177-4f7f-ab7c-4d8e2698109a" facs="#m-7e8aaf03-4abf-4df4-ab9a-3dfd472ea590" label="text-like">by the people.</l><l xml:id="m-6cc0b044-b8e5-4f03-a1d4-660fd8440b6b" facs="#m-ae34aa88-c093-4917-a8ce-fb21e347f3b2" label="text-like">The sacred ministers Ior the serversl accompany the celebrant for both the</l><l xml:id="m-168bac8a-e143-436f-b52c-6a388bc7a42e" facs="#m-76424755-5b55-4d83-bca5-ae0bcfd0aa22" label="text-like">aspersion and the censing of the palms, holding up the edre of his cope.</l><l xml:id="m-5f6d6405-ceec-42e4-9ace-29309f3cec07" facs="#m-282f6715-4fa5-4a49-ac77-29d04d9eddda" label="lyrics-like">à nhe rubrie printed in square brackets concem churches where a deacon and subdeacon</l><l xml:id="m-a9bf7487-f11b-47d6-8406-c65ce3f7f44e" facs="#m-28487012-678a-414a-93dd-091089fc4980" label="text-like">are not available.</l></lg>
            </div>
          </section>
        </score>
      </mdiv>
    </body>
  </music>
</mei>